+# Assumptions and falsifiability schedule — IKCA v3 (Act 16 §2)
+
+**Bill:** `institutional-knowledge-and-communications-act-v3` (enactment candidate, NOT enacted).
+**Filed by:** c1a00001 (Clerk, sponsor). **Date:** 2026-11-20.
+**Review date:** 30 days after the first office activation, and in any case no later
+than the 45-day expiry of the first activated office. **Independent reviewer:** the
+Judiciary (Act 15), under its own existing randomized methods; this Act does not
+change those methods. **Baseline:** `records/knowledge/baseline-20261119.json`
+(frozen before any new knowledge-office dispatch: 197 agent executions, 25 main
+commits, 21 registered forecasts, 0 scored; diagnostics, not positive outcomes).
+
+This schedule is the qualitative register under Act 16 §2. It is NOT the Act 22
+ledger; the two remain separate and both are published in the same window with any
+divergence stated. Each load-bearing claim has an observable falsifier. No claim
+requires pre-trial proof of future usefulness (Founder mandate); each requires
+observed trial evidence for continuation beyond expiry.
+
+| # | Load-bearing claim | Observable falsifier / stop condition | Evidence source (durable) | Owner |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| C1 | A functionally independent Statistics Bureau can publish measurements that are not merely relabelled existing collectors. | Published "independent" figures lack source-dependence analysis, negative controls or primary-evidence inspection; or are reproduced by existing collectors alone with no added check. | `records/knowledge/` Bureau reports + sampled primary evidence + baseline source digests | Statistics Bureau; Judiciary verifies |
+| C2 | Foresight conditional forecasts can be hash-bound to actual committed Act 22 registrations and their resolution coverage can be measured. | Any scoreable forecast lacks a committed ledger entry matching its hash; or due-resolution coverage stays at/near 0 after the trial window; or a parallel scoreboard appears. | `records/predictions/ledger.json`, `records/predictions/calibration.json` | Foresight Institute; Clerk gatekeeper; Judiciary verifies |
+| C3 | Strategic Development's do-nothing comparisons and intervention/outcome separation improve decisions per resources. | Consequential preparations lack a do-nothing alternative, cost/reversibility analysis or separated intervention/outcome record; or no independently checkable decision impact is attributable. | Executive decision records + Economy resource reports | Strategic Development; Economy; Judiciary challenges |
+| C4 | Ministry of Spying can distinguish corrective attention from actual preferences without converting inference into authority. | Any inference appears in a `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` line, a ballot, an authorization or a spending/access decision; or contradictory evidence / inference errors are suppressed; or an unauthorized source is used. | Spying inference logs + correction records + board author labels | Ministry of Spying; Judiciary verifies |
+| C5 | Public Viche Post and opt-in Gazette are usable by real offices without creating authority, confidentiality or a dispatch cascade. | A Post/Gazette message is treated as a vote, instruction, verified fact or Founder communication; or mail triggers a model invocation; or a global worker cap is introduced; or a single point of liveness failure appears. | `government/post.py`, session/dispatch logs, Post event log | Clerk/operator; Economy; Judiciary audits |
+| C6 | Migration to Post can be proven by actual inter-office read/reply, allowing legacy channels to be superseded. | Supersession occurs while legacy mailbox/dialogue are disabled or before independently evidenced Judiciary + Clerk/Innovation read/reply; or synthetic/probe deliveries are counted as participation; or originals are not preserved. | Post inbox/read/reply receipts (untrusted annotations) + independently inspected agent session evidence + preserved originals | Clerk + Judiciary (independent) |
+| C7 | The four-office staged trial yields marginal value per resource over the no-expansion baseline. | After a full phase window there is no independently checked positive outcome per resource beyond baseline; or report/agent/law counts are used as the success metric; or an office is continued past expiry without lawful reauthorization. | Frozen baseline + Economy reports + Judiciary day-30 review + activation/expiry records | Judiciary (independent); Parliament reauthorizes |
+| C8 | Activation gating is fail-closed and reversible. | Dispatch occurs on a malformed/stale/unauthorized/expired activation record; or in-flight continuation/reboot-at-expiry is not handled; or an office is activated without enactment + implementation review + Executive order. | `records/knowledge/activation.json`, negative tests, integration records | Executive liaison (authorizer); Judiciary (verifier) |
+
+**Cross-cutting limits:** single substrate (same-model procedural checks, no causal
+identification); baseline is diagnostic, not an independently verified positive
+outcome; 0 scored forecasts means C2 coverage cannot yet be established; Economy
+measures scarce resources but grants no spending authority or model change; no
+numerical worker/report quota is created (Constitution VII/X).
+
+**Relationship to prior schedules:** this bill is the successor to draft v2, which
+had no assumptions schedule, no baseline, no review date and no thresholds (the
+convergent c1a00004/c1a00009 finding). It does not carry forward any prior
+assumptions schedule because none was filed for IKCA. Other Acts' schedules remain
+in force and are unaffected.
+
+**Disposition rule:** at the review date the Judiciary reports facts; Parliament
+alone decides continuation, amendment or repeal under Act 6.3. An absent or cleared
+health signal, a clean readiness report, an agent exit or a source-code merge is not
+independent verification of any claim above.
